You can't assume that any given site doesn't have a restrictive inbound
feed policy and a nothing-ever-expires policy, which is functionally
equivalent to it being a (limited) archive.

Also, X-no-archive is essentially useless if you post worthwhile or
contentious content, because overall, enough of your output will
probably get quoted for people to get an idea of what you think about
things you discuss via netnews.

If you don't want to be readily trackable via netnews archives, don't post
under your real name.

